      "disposition_reason": "lens-security round 2: engine stderr reaches the terminal, a non-zero exit prints the engine's own code and the script exits 1 without recording; a 143 KB ASCII prompt was delivered on stdin in argument mode",
      "first_seen_round": 1,
      "id": "F-371d23fd",
      "line": 40,
      "message": "The engine's stderr is discarded and set -e exits on its failure, so an auth error, a missing binary, or a prompt over Linux's 128 KiB single-argument limit (this task's diff alone is 75 KB, passed as one argv) ends the script with the engine's exit code and no message; the operator cannot tell why no report was recorded.",
      "minimal_fix": "drop 2>/dev/null on lines 38 and 40 (and prefer --stdin when the prompt exceeds ~100 KB)",
