      "id": "F-47a5db9e",
      "line": 40,
      "message": "`${#prompt}` counts characters under a UTF-8 locale, so a Cyrillic-heavy prompt of 92,271 characters / 151,191 bytes took the argument branch under LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8 and exceeds Linux's 131,072-byte per-argument cap; the run then fails loudly with 'Argument list too long' instead of the stdin fallback the comment promises.",
